#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "feature.*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:6
msgid ""
"The config settings that start with `feature.` modify the defaults of a "
"group of other config settings. These groups are created by the Git "
"developer community as recommended defaults and are subject to change.  In "
"particular, new config options may be added with different defaults."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "feature.experimental"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:14
msgid ""
"Enable config options that are new to Git, and are being considered for "
"future defaults. Config settings included here may be added or removed with "
"each release, including minor version updates. These settings may have "
"unintended interactions since they are so new. Please enable this setting if "
"you are interested in providing feedback on experimental features. The new "
"default values are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:17
msgid ""
"`fetch.negotiationAlgorithm=skipping` may improve fetch negotiation times by "
"skipping more commits at a time, reducing the number of round trips."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:20
msgid ""
"`pack.useBitmapBoundaryTraversal=true` may improve bitmap traversal times by "
"walking fewer objects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:23
msgid ""
"`pack.allowPackReuse=multi` may improve the time it takes to create a pack "
"by reusing objects from multiple packs instead of just one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:27
msgid ""
"`pack.usePathWalk` may speed up packfile creation and make the packfiles be "
"significantly smaller in the presence of certain filename collisions with "
"Git's default name-hash."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:33
msgid ""
"`init.defaultRefFormat=reftable` causes newly initialized repositories to "
"use the reftable format for storing references. This new format solves "
"issues with case-insensitive filesystems, compresses better and performs "
"significantly better with many use cases. Refer to "
"Documentation/technical/reftable.adoc for more information on this new "
"storage format."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "feature.manyFiles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:38
msgid ""
"Enable config options that optimize for repos with many files in the working "
"directory. With many files, commands such as `git status` and `git checkout` "
"may be slow and these new defaults improve performance:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:43
msgid ""
"`index.skipHash=true` speeds up index writes by not computing a trailing "
"checksum. Note that this will cause Git versions earlier than 2.13.0 to "
"refuse to parse the index and Git versions earlier than 2.40.0 will report a "
"corrupted index during `git fsck`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:45
msgid "`index.version=4` enables path-prefix compression in the index."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/feature.adoc:47
msgid ""
"`core.untrackedCache=true` enables the untracked cache. This setting assumes "
"that mtime is working on your machine."
msgstr ""
